@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

title test-workflow — Risk-Aware Verification and Test Quality Gate

start
:Read requirement / Slice acceptance criteria / changed behavior;
:Build Acceptance-to-Test Matrix;
:Select mandatory risk dimensions;

:Static / type / lint / schema checks;
if (Useful failure?) then (yes)
  :Classify root cause;
  stop
endif

:Focused unit / component / API tests;
if (Useful failure?) then (yes)
  :Classify root cause;
  stop
endif

:Boundary + negative-path checks;
:Assert failure/error contract
format + structure + semantics + caller consumability;

if (Complex input space or strong invariant?) then (yes)
  :Property / fuzz checks;
endif

if (External or multi-module boundary touched?) then (yes)
  :Integration / contract checks;
endif

if (Real entrypoint / config / client policy risk?) then (yes)
  :Real URL / proxy / TLS / cookie / header / cache checks;
endif

if (High-risk logic or weak-test suspicion?) then (yes)
  :Targeted mutation / test-strength check;
endif

:Affected regression;

if (Critical browser-visible flow?) then (yes)
  :Browser / E2E;
endif

if (Nondeterminism risk or intermittent failure?) then (yes)
  :Isolation / flaky diagnosis;
endif

:Evaluate Test Quality Gate;

if (Every acceptance criterion, mandatory dimension\nand failure/error contract satisfied?) then (yes)
  :PASS;
else (no)
  :FAIL / PARTIAL / BLOCKED;
endif
stop

note right
Coverage is diagnostic only.
N/A requires a concrete reason.
Failure/status/exception occurrence alone is not PASS.
Real boundary behavior must use real or production-like entrypoints.
FAIL then retry PASS without a verified external cause is flaky, not PASS.
end note
@enduml
